# Dawnhand Dissident: "During your turn, you may cast creature spells from among cards you own exiled with this creature ..." The
# permission changes no timing (the rulings): a creature with flash may be cast from exile at instant speed (CR 702.8a), but only
# during its controller's turn. Bot1 surveils its Cathar Commando into the graveyard on turn three (blighting the Dissident itself,
# 0/1) and exiles it on turn five (blighting its Sylvan Caryatid twice, 0/1): three -1/-1 counters among its creatures. On Bot2's
# turn six, with {W}{W} open and the counters there, the Commando can't be cast from exile; in Bot1's upkeep on turn seven it is,
# with flash, removing the three counters (CR 118.8): the Dissident and the Caryatid are back to 1/2 and 0/3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Dawnhand Dissident
Forest
Mox Emerald
Sylvan Caryatid
Plains
Mox Pearl
Plains
Cathar Commando
Plains x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

